      "text": "class Point2d {\npublic:\nPoint2d( float x = 0.0, float y = 0.0 )\n: _x( x ), _y( y ) {};\n// access functions for x & y same as above\n// invariant across type: not made virtual\n// add placeholders for z — do nothing ...\nvirtual float z(){ return 0.0 };\nvirtual void z( float ) {}\n// turn type explicit operations virtual\nvirtual void\noperator+=( const Point2d& rhs ) {\n_x += rhs.x(); _y += rhs.y(); }\n// ... more members\nprotected:\nfloat _x, _y;\n};\n\nclass Point3d : public Point2d {\npublic:\nPoint3d( float x = 0.0, float y = 0.0, float z = 0.0 )\n: Point2d( x, y ), _z( z ) {};\nfloat z() { return _z; }\nvoid z( float newZ ) { _z = newZ; }\nvoid operator+=( const Point2d& rhs ) {\nPoint2d::operator+=( rhs );\n_z += rhs.z();\n}\n// ... more members\nprotected:\nfloat _z;\n};",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "class Point2d {\npublic:\nPoint2d( float x = 0.0, float y = 0.0 )\n: _x( x ), _y( y ) {};\n// access functions for x & y same as above\n// invariant across type: not made virtual\n// add placeholders for z — do nothing ...\nvirtual float z(){ return 0.0 };\nvirtual void z( float ) {}\n// turn type explicit operations virtual\nvirtual void\noperator+=( const Point2d& rhs ) {\n_x += rhs.x(); _y += rhs.y(); }\n// ... more members\nprotected:\nfloat _x, _y;\n};\n\nclass Point3d : public Point2d {\npublic:\nPoint3d( float x = 0.0, float y = 0.0, float z = 0.0 )\n: Point2d( x, y ), _z( z ) {};\nfloat z() { return _z; }\nvoid z( float newZ ) { _z = newZ; }\nvoid operator+=( const Point2d& rhs ) {\nPoint2d::operator+=( rhs );\n_z += rhs.z();\n}\n// ... more members\nprotected:\nfloat _z;\n};",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "VRE4WeyVwJVpyT_z9-RKp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 966.5475732712523,
      "y": 1014.309539068312,
      "width": 833.1195068359375,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dotted",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "Q-vwWJ4wOp8xcu7sP8nt_",
      "index": "b5dl",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 608152087,
      "version": 165,
      "versionNonce": 996101303,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1777339156779,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Introduction of a virtual table associated with Point2d to hold the address of\neach virtual function it declares. The size of this table in general is the number\nof virtual functions declared plus an additional one or two slots to support\nruntime type identification.\n\n2. Introduction of the vptr within each class object. The vptr provides the runtime\nlink for an object to efficiently find its associated virtual table.\n\n3. Augmentation of the constructor to initialize the object's vptr to the virtual\ntable of the class. Depending on the aggressiveness of the compiler's\noptimization, this may mean resetting the vptr within the derived and each\nbase class constructor. (This is discussed in more detail in Chapter 5.)\n\n4. Augmentation of the destructor to reset the vptr to the associated virtual table\nof the class. (It is likely to have been set to address the virtual table of the\nderived class within the destructor of the derived class. Remember, the order\nof destructor calls is in reverse: derived class and then base class.) An\naggressive optimizing compiler can suppress a great many of these assignments.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Introduction of a virtual table associated with Point2d to hold the address of\neach virtual function it declares. The size of this table in general is the number\nof virtual functions declared plus an additional one or two slots to support\nruntime type identification.\n\n2. Introduction of the vptr within each class object. The vptr provides the runtime\nlink for an object to efficiently find its associated virtual table.\n\n3. Augmentation of the constructor to initialize the object's vptr to the virtual\ntable of the class. Depending on the aggressiveness of the compiler's\noptimization, this may mean resetting the vptr within the derived and each\nbase class constructor. (This is discussed in more detail in Chapter 5.)\n\n4. Augmentation of the destructor to reset the vptr to the associated virtual table\nof the class. (It is likely to have been set to address the virtual table of the\nderived class within the destructor of the derived class. Remember, the order\nof destructor calls is in reverse: derived class and then base class.) An\naggressive optimizing compiler can suppress a great many of these assignments.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "5p7oZmmY89elpWn4_8lJV",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1848.3332875569668,
      "y": 1018.5952533540267,
      "width": 374,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dotted",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "Q-vwWJ4wOp8xcu7sP8nt_",
      "index": "b5dz",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 878495287,
      "version": 362,
      "versionNonce": 1902288343,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1777339156779,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "struct no_virts {\nint d1, d2;\n};\nclass has_virts: public no_virts {\npublic:\nvirtual void foo();\n// ...\nprivate:\nint d3;\n};\nno_virts *p = new has_virts;",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "struct no_virts {\nint d1, d2;\n};\nclass has_virts: public no_virts {\npublic:\nvirtual void foo();\n// ...\nprivate:\nint d3;\n};\nno_virts *p = new has_virts;",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "EVuyhBBCBJ_AP1dSu2H_Y",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1850.8332875569668,
      "y": 1311.0952533540267,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dotted",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "Q-vwWJ4wOp8xcu7sP8nt_",
      "index": "b5dzV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1208016823,
      "version": 130,
      "versionNonce": 1763625719,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1777339156779,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Vptr Placement at End of Class",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Vptr Placement at End of Class",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "_uFaohukcS4fwkkypYm4t",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1832.0832875569668,
      "y": 1594.8452533540267,
      "width": 352,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dotted",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "Q-vwWJ4wOp8xcu7sP8nt_",
      "index": "b5dzl",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1891674777,
      "version": 377,
      "versionNonce": 790123543,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1777339156779,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Vptr Placement at Front of Class",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Vptr Placement at Front of Class",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "jIbUgyyr3wxCys_ymh1Eo",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1394.5832875569668,
      "y": 1529.8452533540267,
      "width": 813.2196044921875,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dotted",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "Q-vwWJ4wOp8xcu7sP8nt_",
      "index": "b5dzx",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1221570425,
      "version": 424,
      "versionNonce": 1262729527,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1777339156779,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Placing the vptr at the end of the class object preserves the object layout of the\nbase class C struct, thus permitting its use within C code.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Placing the vptr at the end of the class object preserves the object layout of the\nbase class C struct, thus permitting its use within C code.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "PmZBhJ1a-VdVPVx8hJkTV",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1105.8332875569668,
      "y": 1707.3452533540267,
      "width": 967.3095092773438,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dotted",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "Q-vwWJ4wOp8xcu7sP8nt_",
      "index": "b5dzz",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2095424665,
      "version": 260,
      "versionNonce": 1392867927,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1777339156779,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Placing the vptr at the start of the class is more efficient in supporting some virtual\nfunction invocations through pointers to class members under multiple inheritance\n(see Section 4.4). Otherwise, not only must the offset to the start of the class be\nmade available at runtime, but also the offset to the location of the vptr of that class\nmust be made available.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Placing the vptr at the start of the class is more efficient in supporting some virtual\nfunction invocations through pointers to class members under multiple inheritance\n(see Section 4.4). Otherwise, not only must the offset to the start of the class be\nmade available at runtime, but also the offset to the location of the vptr of that class\nmust be made available.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
